---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
import { BadgeEarnedModalListener } from '../components/gamification/BadgeEarnedModalListener';
import { FollowPackFinder } from '../components/follow-pack';
import { getAccountCount, getCategoryCounts } from '../data/follow-pack';
import { getCategoryGroupsWithCounts } from '../data/follow-pack/localize';
import { PUBLISH_RELAYS } from '../components/follow-pack/starterPackEvent';

// Counts are derived from the dataset at build time — never hardcoded, so the
// page cannot drift from the data the way the old "100+" copy did (the real
// number has been in the hundreds for months).
const accountCount = getAccountCount();
const categoryCounts = getCategoryCounts();
const groups = getCategoryGroupsWithCounts(categoryCounts, 'en');
const categoryCount = groups.reduce((total, group) => total + group.categories.length, 0);

// Query-matched <title> (docs/audit-2026-07/market-research.md §6 row 11:
// "how to find people to follow on nostr" — page 1 is a GitHub README).
// The friendly on-page H1 below is independent of this.
// Titled for the tool it is, not the question it used to duplicate. This read
// "How to Find People to Follow on Nostr" against
// /guides/finding-community's "How to Find People to Follow on Nostr (2026)" —
// two URLs competing for one query while serving different intents: that guide
// teaches strategies, this page hands you a vetted list to import.
// accountCount is interpolated so the number can never drift from the data.
const title = `Nostr Follow Pack: ${accountCount} Accounts to Start With`;
const description = `Start your Nostr feed with ${accountCount} curated accounts across ${categoryCount} categories. Pick the ones you like and import them into any client: paste the list, or publish it and scan a QR code.`;
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 lg:py-16">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
          <p class="text-micro uppercase text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mb-4">
            The last step of the guide
          </p>

          <h1 class="text-display font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-6">
            You made an account. Now fill the feed
          </h1>

          <p class="text-lead text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-8 max-w-measure mx-auto">
            {accountCount} hand-checked Nostr accounts, sorted into {categoryCount} categories.
            A starter set of {categoryCounts.jumpstart} essentials, then photographers,
            homesteaders, musicians, shops that take Lightning. Tick the ones that look
            interesting and import them into any client: paste the list, or publish it and
            scan a QR code.
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-body-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-success-600 dark:text-success-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m4.5 12.75 6 6 9-13.5" />
              </svg>
              Free, no registration
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-success-600 dark:text-success-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m4.5 12.75 6 6 9-13.5" />
              </svg>
              Works with every client
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-success-600 dark:text-success-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m4.5 12.75 6 6 9-13.5" />
              </svg>
              Nothing is published unless you ask
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why this page exists -->
    <section class="py-12 lg:py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
            An empty feed is the number one reason beginners quit
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-4 text-body text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
            <p>
              Nostr has no algorithm deciding what you see. That is the point, and it is also
              why the first five minutes feel broken. You sign up, open a client, and the
              timeline is blank. Nothing recommends anyone. Most people conclude the network is
              dead and never come back.
            </p>
            <p>
              It is not dead. You just follow nobody yet. Following 20-50 active accounts is
              the difference between a blank screen and a network that looks alive, and it is
              the one step no client does for you.
            </p>
            <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
              That is what this page is for. Browse, tick the accounts that look interesting,
              and leave with a list you can import anywhere.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <p class="font-display text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">{accountCount}</p>
              <p class="text-caption text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">curated accounts</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <p class="font-display text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">{categoryCount}</p>
              <p class="text-caption text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">categories, all populated</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <p class="font-display text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">20-50</p>
              <p class="text-caption text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">a good first pack</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Browse by category (server-rendered: real ids, real counts) -->
    <section class="py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Browse by category
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-10">
            Every category below has accounts in it, and the number tells you how many. Pick one
            to open the finder pre-filtered, or scroll on and search the whole set.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-10">
            {groups.map(group => (
              <div>
                <div class="mb-4">
                  <h3 class="text-h3 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
                    {group.name}
                    <span class="ms-2 text-caption font-normal text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
                      {group.count} accounts
                    </span>
                  </h3>
                  <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">{group.description}</p>
                </div>

                <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                  {group.categories.map(category => (
                    <a
                      href={`/follow-pack?category=${category.id}#find`}
                      class="block p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 transition-colors hover:border-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:border-gray-700 dark:hover:bg-gray-800"
                    >
                      <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div class="min-w-0">
                          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
                            {category.name}
                          </p>
                          <p class="mt-1 text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                            {category.description}
                          </p>
                        </div>
                        <span class="flex-shrink-0 px-2 py-1 rounded-full text-caption font-semibold text-gray-600 bg-gray-100 dark:text-gray-300 dark:bg-gray-800">
                          {category.count}
                        </span>
                      </div>
                    </a>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main Tool Section -->
    <section id="find" class="py-8 lg:py-12 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 scroll-mt-20">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">
            Pick your accounts
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-6">
            Filter by category or search all {accountCount} of them. Your picks are remembered
            in this browser, so you can come back and finish later.
          </p>
          <FollowPackFinder client:idle />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How It Works -->
    <section class="py-16">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-center mb-12">
            How it works
          </h2>

          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
            <div class="text-center">
              <p class="mb-2 text-micro uppercase text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true">1</p>
              <h3 class="text-h3 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Browse and select</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Filter {accountCount} accounts by category, then hit "Follow" on the ones you
                find interesting. Nothing happens on the network yet.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="text-center">
              <p class="mb-2 text-micro uppercase text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true">2</p>
              <h3 class="text-h3 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Build your pack</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Aim for 20-50 accounts across a few categories. The sidebar shows the mix you
                have picked so far.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="text-center">
              <p class="mb-2 text-micro uppercase text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true">3</p>
              <h3 class="text-h3 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Export and import</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Take a QR code, a plain npub list, or a NIP-02 file into Amethyst, Damus,
                Coracle, Primal or any other client.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    <section class="py-16 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-center mb-8">
            Frequently asked questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <h3 class="text-h4 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Is this free to use?</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Yes. No registration, no account, no tracking. It exists because the empty
                first feed is where most newcomers give up.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <h3 class="text-h4 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">How do I import into my client?</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Copy the npub list and paste it into the client's "Import follows" feature.
                Or publish the pack and scan its QR code. Works with Amethyst, Damus,
                Coracle, Primal and more.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <h3 class="text-h4 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">How many accounts should I follow?</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Start with 20-50. That is enough for a feed that moves without being
                overwhelming, and you will find more people on your own once you are in.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <h3 class="text-h4 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Who curated these accounts, and how?</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                The list was assembled from public Nostr follow packs, then checked by hand for
                activity and topic fit: {accountCount} accounts across {categoryCount}
                categories. It is a starting point, not a ranking. No vetting authority stands
                behind it and no account is endorsed. Want to suggest one, or have yours
                removed? Open an issue on GitHub.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <h3 class="text-h4 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Will my selections be saved?</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Yes, in this browser's local storage, so your pack is still here when you come
                back. Nothing is sent anywhere. No account is required and no server of ours
                holds your picks.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900">
              <h3 class="text-h4 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Does anything get published to Nostr?</h3>
              <p class="text-body-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
                Only if you explicitly ask for it. The QR code, npub list and NIP-02 export all
                run inside your browser and touch no network. The export dialog also offers one
                optional extra: publishing your pack as a public NIP-51 list to
                {' '}{PUBLISH_RELAYS.length} public relays ({PUBLISH_RELAYS.join(', ')}). That
                step names the relays, shows you exactly what the event contains, and needs a
                separate confirmation, because a published list is public and effectively
                permanent.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA Section -->
    <section class="py-16 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center">
          <h2 class="text-h2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">
            Ready to fill that feed?
          </h2>

          <p class="text-body text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-8">
            {categoryCounts.jumpstart} accounts in the starter set alone. Pick a handful and
            your timeline stops being empty today.
          </p>

          <a
            href="#find"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-primary-600 text-white rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-primary-700 transition-colors"
          >
            Start picking accounts
            <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
  <!-- Badge celebrations can fire from this page (key generation / follows / import) -->
  <BadgeEarnedModalListener client:only="react" />
</Layout>
